Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:24:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Swapping firmware on the PicoFox: the vendor target fetches
 the vendor's .uf2 (pfoxr3v1 / forceformat) from its GitHub into the browser,
 a loaded image belongs to the target it was loaded for (switching targets
 forgets it, so the wrong image cannot be flashed), the flash result says what
 comes back per image, opening a drive whose files belong to the other
 firmware says so in both directions, the firmware no longer relabels an
 inherited volume (the vendor side could not undo it); README: how to switch

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AwviighMTcaTHg8tykZaoh
